; Export list for rxpshim.dll (Windows only).
;
; On Windows, `extern "C"` is NOT enough to export a symbol from a DLL -- it
; only fixes the name mangling. Without an export list the shim compiles and
; links cleanly and produces a DLL that exports nothing at all, and the failure
; surfaces much later as ctypes' "function 'rxpshim_collect_misses' not found".
;
; This lives in a .def rather than as __declspec(dllexport) in rxp_shim.cpp so
; that the shim source stays byte-identical across platforms: the Linux/macOS
; container build relies on default ELF visibility and must not change.
;
; Keep in sync with the extern "C" block at the bottom of rxp_shim.cpp.
EXPORTS
rxpshim_collect_misses
rxpshim_error
rxpshim_miss_count
rxpshim_shot_count
rxpshim_hit_shot_count
rxpshim_echo_count
rxpshim_copy
rxpshim_free
